1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,664
After the Last Bell.

2
00:00:01,664 --> 00:00:04,189
Episode One: The Boy Who Borrowed Tomorrow.

3
00:00:04,189 --> 00:00:06,715
Above Johannesburg, cars floated past the rooftops.

4
00:00:06,715 --> 00:00:08,666
Rain climbed into the clouds.

5
00:00:08,666 --> 00:00:11,478
Lebo hung from a bridge with one hand.

6
00:00:11,478 --> 00:00:14,577
In the other, he held a cracked brass watch.

7
00:00:14,577 --> 00:00:18,537
A girl in a red blazer stood where gravity said she shouldn't.

8
00:00:18,537 --> 00:00:22,497
I told you not to wish for a better day, she said.

9
00:00:22,497 --> 00:00:25,309
Seven hours earlier, the world still made sense.

10
00:00:25,309 --> 00:00:26,112
Mostly.

11
00:00:26,112 --> 00:00:30,072
Lebo sat in his kitchen, repairing his school bag with a fork.

12
00:00:30,072 --> 00:00:32,884
His little sister, Naledi, watched the zip break.

13
00:00:32,884 --> 00:00:35,696
You know the fork is losing, she said.

14
00:00:35,696 --> 00:00:37,361
Strategic retreat, Lebo replied.

15
00:00:37,361 --> 00:00:39,886
She gave him a folded paper star.

16
00:00:39,886 --> 00:00:40,976
For luck.

17
00:00:40,976 --> 00:00:43,501
And don't forget my solar system project.

18
00:00:43,501 --> 00:00:46,026
Lebo tucked the star into his blazer.

19
00:00:46,026 --> 00:00:48,838
On his phone waited a scholarship interview reminder.

20
00:00:48,838 --> 00:00:49,929
Three o'clock.

21
00:00:49,929 --> 00:00:51,306
No late arrivals.

22
00:00:51,306 --> 00:00:54,979
This was his chance to change things for both of them.

23
00:00:54,979 --> 00:00:56,930
He ran into the afternoon.

24
00:00:56,930 --> 00:00:59,456
His best friend Tumi called with advice.

25
00:00:59,456 --> 00:01:02,555
Walk in like they already gave you the scholarship.

26
00:01:02,555 --> 00:01:05,654
At this rate, Lebo said, I'm walking in tomorrow.

27
00:01:05,654 --> 00:01:08,179
He took a shortcut into an alley.

28
00:01:08,179 --> 00:01:10,704
Suddenly, every sound in the city stopped.

29
00:01:10,704 --> 00:01:14,407
Beneath a yellow umbrella, an old woman sat surrounded by watches.

30
00:01:14,407 --> 00:01:16,085
Not one was ticking.

31
00:01:16,085 --> 00:01:17,763
You're late, she said.

32
00:01:17,763 --> 00:01:20,020
Apparently that's public information, Lebo answered.

33
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:22,855
She placed a brass watch on the counter.

34
00:01:22,855 --> 00:01:24,823
Its face had thirteen marks.

35
00:01:24,823 --> 00:01:26,790
One minute, she told him.

36
00:01:26,790 --> 00:01:28,179
Yours to repeat.

37
00:01:28,179 --> 00:01:29,278
How much?

38
00:01:29,278 --> 00:01:30,378
A minute.

39
00:01:30,378 --> 00:01:34,081
He turned to leave, but his broken bag caught the stall.

40
00:01:34,081 --> 00:01:35,470
His papers scattered.

41
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:37,437
The woman helped gather them.

42
00:01:37,437 --> 00:01:41,719
Among the school reports was Naledi's drawing: two stick figures standing on Saturn.

43
00:01:41,719 --> 00:01:44,555
Someone is expecting you home, the woman said.

44
00:01:44,555 --> 00:01:47,390
Then don't spend more than you can afford.

45
00:01:47,390 --> 00:01:49,936
She pressed the watch into his hand.

46
00:01:49,936 --> 00:01:51,325
A taxi hooted.

47
00:01:51,325 --> 00:01:53,582
Lebo looked away for a moment.

48
00:01:53,582 --> 00:01:56,417
When he looked back, the stall was gone.

49
00:01:56,417 --> 00:01:59,542
He reached the interview at one minute past three.

50
00:01:59,542 --> 00:02:01,509
The receptionist closed her folder.

51
00:02:01,509 --> 00:02:02,608
I'm sorry.

52
00:02:02,608 --> 00:02:05,155
The panel has started its final review.

53
00:02:05,155 --> 00:02:07,701
In his pocket, the watch grew warm.

54
00:02:07,701 --> 00:02:09,957
Two words appeared across the glass.

55
00:02:09,957 --> 00:02:11,057
Turn back.

56
00:02:11,057 --> 00:02:12,735
Lebo turned the crown.

57
00:02:12,735 --> 00:02:14,702
Water rose into a jug.

58
00:02:14,702 --> 00:02:16,670
A printer swallowed a page.

59
00:02:16,670 --> 00:02:19,505
And suddenly he stood outside the office again.

60
00:02:19,505 --> 00:02:20,894
Three o'clock exactly.

61
00:02:20,894 --> 00:02:23,150
Just in time, the receptionist said.

62
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:24,250
Lebo smiled.

63
00:02:24,250 --> 00:02:28,532
In the glass behind him, a faceless figure wearing his uniform smiled back.

64
00:02:28,532 --> 00:02:31,787
The interview went better than he had dared to hope.

65
00:02:31,787 --> 00:02:37,526
Outside, Lebo was already recording a message to Tumi when a girl in a red blazer blocked his path.

66
00:02:37,526 --> 00:02:39,126
Her name was Aya.

67
00:02:39,126 --> 00:02:41,829
Her shadow moved a moment after she did.

68
00:02:41,829 --> 00:02:43,981
Show me your hands, she said.

69
00:02:43,981 --> 00:02:47,512
Beneath the skin of Lebo's finger was a thin black ring.

70
00:02:47,512 --> 00:02:48,837
How many turns?

71
00:02:48,837 --> 00:02:49,885
Just one.

72
00:02:49,885 --> 00:02:53,416
Then every phone on the street rang like a school bell.

73
00:02:53,416 --> 00:02:55,292
Don't answer yours, Aya warned.

74
00:02:55,292 --> 00:02:57,168
But the screen said Naledi.

75
00:02:57,168 --> 00:02:58,217
Lebo answered.

76
00:02:58,217 --> 00:03:00,093
The voice wasn't his sister's.

77
00:03:00,093 --> 00:03:01,693
It was his own.

78
00:03:01,693 --> 00:03:02,465
Older.

79
00:03:02,465 --> 00:03:03,238
Exhausted.

80
00:03:03,238 --> 00:03:06,493
Whatever she tells you, don't let her take the watch.

81
00:03:06,493 --> 00:03:07,817
The call ended.

82
00:03:07,817 --> 00:03:08,866
Traffic froze.

83
00:03:08,866 --> 00:03:11,293
A dropped coin stopped above the road.

84
00:03:11,293 --> 00:03:13,721
Something stepped out of a glass window.

85
00:03:13,721 --> 00:03:15,873
A faceless student, dripping black sand.

86
00:03:15,873 --> 00:03:17,749
One minute borrowed, it whispered.

87
00:03:17,749 --> 00:03:19,073
One tomorrow due.

88
00:03:19,073 --> 00:03:23,708
Aya opened her case and drew a sword shaped like the hand of a clock.

89
00:03:23,708 --> 00:03:24,481
Run!

90
00:03:24,481 --> 00:03:26,081
Lebo took three steps.

91
00:03:26,081 --> 00:03:30,440
Then he saw the creature's shadow reaching for a little boy beside a taxi.

92
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:32,867
The child's shoe began crumbling to dust.

93
00:03:32,867 --> 00:03:36,675
It takes the nearest tomorrow if it can't get yours, Aya shouted.

94
00:03:36,675 --> 00:03:38,551
Lebo looked at the watch.

95
00:03:38,551 --> 00:03:39,875
He could run.

96
00:03:39,875 --> 00:03:41,475
He could save himself.

97
00:03:41,475 --> 00:03:43,627
Instead, he turned the crown again.

98
00:03:43,627 --> 00:03:45,742
The phone rang in his hand.

99
00:03:45,742 --> 00:03:47,857
This time, Lebo threw it away.

100
00:03:47,857 --> 00:03:49,700
The boy by the taxi!

101
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:50,731
Left ankle!

102
00:03:50,731 --> 00:03:52,574
Aya moved without questioning him.

103
00:03:52,574 --> 00:03:55,503
Her blade pinned the creature's shadow to the street.

104
00:03:55,503 --> 00:03:58,160
A second black ring appeared on Lebo's hand.

105
00:03:58,160 --> 00:03:59,461
The watch cracked.

106
00:03:59,461 --> 00:04:02,661
Above the city, an enormous clock emerged through the clouds.

107
00:04:02,661 --> 00:04:04,233
Its hands moved backward.

108
00:04:04,233 --> 00:04:06,077
Aya looked up in fear.

109
00:04:06,077 --> 00:04:07,921
That isn't supposed to happen.

110
00:04:07,921 --> 00:04:09,222
The road tilted.

111
00:04:09,222 --> 00:04:10,253
Cars lifted.

112
00:04:10,253 --> 00:04:11,283
Rain rose.

113
00:04:11,283 --> 00:04:14,482
Aya caught Lebo's sleeve and pulled him toward a bridge.

114
00:04:14,482 --> 00:04:17,953
He grabbed the railing as the city fell into the sky.

115
00:04:17,953 --> 00:04:21,152
Now he was hanging over everything he had ever known.

116
00:04:21,152 --> 00:04:24,894
I told you not to wish for a better day, Aya said.

117
00:04:24,894 --> 00:04:27,822
In my defence, Lebo answered, this is definitely different.

118
00:04:27,822 --> 00:04:29,395
The watch struck thirteen.

119
00:04:29,395 --> 00:04:31,781
Naledi's paper star slipped from his pocket.

120
00:04:31,781 --> 00:04:33,082
He caught it.

121
00:04:33,082 --> 00:04:35,739
Inside were three words in her careful handwriting.

122
00:04:35,739 --> 00:04:37,041
Come home, idiot.

123
00:04:37,041 --> 00:04:38,342
The watch opened.

124
00:04:38,342 --> 00:04:39,915
There were no gears.

125
00:04:39,915 --> 00:04:42,030
Only a window into his kitchen.

126
00:04:42,030 --> 00:04:44,145
Naledi sat beside her painted planets.

127
00:04:44,145 --> 00:04:45,988
A shadow stood behind her.

128
00:04:45,988 --> 00:04:47,832
Payment accepted, whispered the creature.

129
00:04:47,832 --> 00:04:49,405
The window went dark.

130
00:04:49,405 --> 00:04:52,333
Tell me how to get her back, Lebo said.

131
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:54,177
Aya offered him her sword.

132
00:04:54,177 --> 00:04:56,292
First, you have to let go.

133
00:04:56,292 --> 00:04:59,762
Far beneath the floating city, a door opened in the sky.

134
00:04:59,762 --> 00:05:01,335
Lebo released the railing.

135
00:05:01,335 --> 00:05:02,636
To be continued.
